			<div class="content" id="post-content-4662226">
									

<p>I'm upvoting, primarily for the masterful use of the ConProcs here to build suspense but there's a few things here that I don't think work as well:</p>
<ul>
<li>Why build a space station orbiting <em>Mercury</em> to study a black hole 5,000 ly away?</li>
<li>I'm not sure why this needs to be a space station or have a contemporary date. If this was either a remote terrestrial radio observatory, or set in the future you wouldn't need to stretch disbelief with this space station, and the astronomers could have been civilians which would IMO be more poignant.</li>
<li>The ending is significantly heavy-handed and comes across as campy to me. FWIW I also hate the ending of <em>Event Horizon</em> for similar reasons, which this reminds me of. I feel like this could have been much more subtle.</li>
</ul>

							</div>

								
